    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085",
      "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
      "finding": "Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) showed low split-half reliability (Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within)). The observed research question was 'Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability'."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-014",
      "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
      "finding": "DRIVE efficiency rises early-to-late (+0.078 G1, +0.093 all games) instead of dropping, contrary to the hypothesis. The observed research question was 'Within-game DRIVE decline by game third'."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-021",
      "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
      "finding": "OTHER play-type increased by +2.26 to +2.48pp in H2 in every bucket; crunch OTHER +6.08pp, PULL_UP +1.20pp at -0.045 PPP; post-run DRIVE +3.75pp, OTHER -6.72pp. The observed research question was 'Within-game tactical adaptation (halftime, crunch, post-run)'."
    }
  ],
  "failed_approaches": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005",
      "what_failed": "Attempting to measure defensive scheme changes within and across games using inferred labels.",
      "why": "Question was untestable due to label or classification error. Inferred labels could not separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently, and transition matrices were near-uniform, consistent with label noise."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085",
      "what_failed": "Attempting to establish 'Connector quality Q_p' as a stable player-season attribute using split-half reliability.",
      "why": "Question was untestable due to low measurement reliability. Split-half r=0.215 (Spearman-Brown 0.355) was too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance was within-player half-to-half."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-021",
      "what_failed": "Descriptive analysis of within-game tactical adaptation (play-type shifts).",
      "why": "The analysis was limited by label or classification error and low measurement reliability, particularly with the 'OTHER' play-type label which was known to be noisy. No inferential tests were performed."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_establishes": [
    "It is challenging to infer and attribute specific defensive effects or adjustments within games, as evidenced by issues with 'inferred labels' for defensive schemes (FAM:SF-APPA-005, FAM:SF-APPM-021).",
    "Low measurement reliability is a significant hurdle for establishing player (and by extension, team) traits as stable or scoutable attributes (FAM:SF-APPS-085).",
    "Within-game offensive efficiency does not necessarily decline; it can even increase from early to late game (FAM:SF-APPS-014), which complicates the assumption that H2-H1 changes are solely due to defensive suppression."
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish": [
    "A direct definition or robust method for measuring 'H2-H1 change' in opponent performance that is cleanly attributable to a defense.",
    "The specific reliability of any proposed 'defense's effect on opponents' H2-H1 change' as a team trait, as the prior work focused on player traits or descriptive analyses.",
    "Whether the available data (120 team-seasons) is sufficient to overcome the low measurement reliability issues observed in similar studies."
  ],
  "own_inferences": [
    "Defining 'defense's effect' in a way that isolates it from offensive adjustments, game flow, score effects, and other confounders will be crucial and difficult.",
    "The 'H2-H1 change' metric itself needs careful construction, potentially accounting for game state (e.g., score differential, opponent strength, home/away advantage) to minimize noise and improve attribution.",
    "Assessing reliability will require multiple data points (e.g., H2-H1 changes) for each team-season, and then comparing these measures across multiple seasons for the same team, which may reduce the effective sample size for reliability calculations."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "The precise definition and calculation of 'H2-H1 change' in opponent performance.",
    "How to effectively attribute observed H2-H1 changes specifically to defensive actions or strategies, rather than other factors.",
    "The number of distinct team-seasons available per team, which is critical for assessing within-team reliability across seasons."
