  "historical_effect": {
    "changed_decision": "yes",
    "explanation": "The historical evidence, particularly FAM:SF-APPA-005 and FAM:SF-APPS-085, significantly increased concerns about the testability of the research question. FAM:SF-APPA-005 highlighted the difficulty and risks (LABEL_ERROR) in attributing within-game changes to defensive adjustments. FAM:SF-APPS-085 demonstrated that even well-defined player traits can have critically low measurement reliability, making them untestable as stable attributes (MEASURE_RELIABILITY). This suggests that establishing 'reliable team trait' for a complex, attributed defensive effect will be very challenging, likely leading to an untestable outcome due to poor measurement reliability and attribution issues. FAM:SF-APPS-014 also showed that within-game offensive performance doesn't always decline, complicating the interpretation of H2-H1 changes."
