      }
    ]
  },
  "prior_work": {
    "already_answered": "no",
    "cited": [],
    "summary": "No prior work has directly answered whether a defense's effect on opponents' H2-H1 change is a reliable team trait. However, related studies have highlighted significant challenges in measuring within-game defensive adjustments and establishing the reliability of complex derived performance metrics, suggesting that this question is likely untestable with similar methodological approaches."
  },
  "risks": [
    {
      "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
      "text": "The primary risk is that the 'defense's effect on opponents' H2-H1 change' will not be a reliable measure, meaning its variance within a team across games/seasons will be greater than its variance between teams. This would make it impossible to establish as a stable 'team trait', as seen with FAM:SF-APPS-085."
    },
