      "code": "LABEL_ERROR",
      "text": "If 'defense's effect' relies on inferred defensive schemes or play-type labels (as suggested by the data description and prior work like FAM:SF-APPA-005, FAM:SF-APPM-021), there's a high risk of label error or noise obscuring any true effect or making it indistinguishable from offensive execution or random variation."
    },
    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "While 120 team-seasons is a decent overall sample, assessing *reliability* at the team level requires multiple observations *per team*. If many teams only have one or two seasons of data, the power to detect a reliable trait across seasons for individual teams will be low, or the effective sample size for reliability coefficients will be small."
    }
