    "estimand": "The Intraclass Correlation Coefficient (ICC) of a team's average 'H2-H1 opponent offensive efficiency change' across multiple seasons. The H2-H1 change for a given game is defined as the difference in opponent Points Per Possession (PPP) in the second half minus opponent PPP in the first half, adjusted for initial score differential and opponent strength. The 'defense's effect' is modeled as the residual of this H2-H1 change after controlling for known offensive factors and game state variables.",
